// ★ THE DECLARATION ATTRIBUTES MUST REACH THE EMITTED C — and for two days they did not.
//
// `[cold]`, `[hot]`, `[allocator]` and `[noreturn]` are the project's claim in miniature: a fact
// the front end knows, handed to the optimizer so it can act on it. The AST emitter wrote them.
// The IR backend never carried them, so deleting src/emit/ on 2026-09-23 dropped all four —
// silently, because:
//
//   · behaviour is identical (three of them are hints, so no program's output changes)
//   · `annot_gate`, the ONLY instrument that compared annotations, was retired in the same commit
//   · `tests/BASELINE.txt` was then recorded from the backend that had already lost them
//
// Three independent ways to not notice, all created at once. The same shape as D-62: a
// representation loss that behaviour cannot see.
//
// ★ AND WHEN THE BASELINE GAINED AN `at=` COLUMN, IT STILL DID NOT BITE — because no corpus
// program used any of these attributes. A column that counts something nothing produces reports
// zero forever. THIS FILE is what makes it bite; removing the emission now moves the baseline.
//
// `[allocator]` and `[noreturn]` are more than hints. `malloc, returns_nonnull` tells the optimizer
// the returned pointer is non-null and aliases nothing, and returning from a `noreturn` function
// is undefined. So `[allocator]` is believed only on an `extern` (a body cannot be checked to
// satisfy it; this file's first version marked a body that returned NULL), and a `[noreturn]`
// body is CHECKED: every return must be unreachable (E135, noreturn_*_fail.ln). On an extern
// both were parsed and dropped until 2026-10-01; they reach the prototype now.
[cold]
func rare_path() i32 {
    return 0
}
[hot]
func inner_loop(x i32) i32 {
    return x +% 1
}
// Never called: the point is that the ATTRIBUTE reaches the C, and the baseline's build step only
// defines libc_printf/libc_puts — a program it cannot link is a program it silently skips, which
// is how the first version of this test failed to protect anything.
[allocator]
extern func fresh(n usize) *var u8
[noreturn]
extern func halt(code i32)
[noreturn]
func die() effects raises {
    panic("die")
}
func main() i32 {
    return rare_path() +% inner_loop(1)
}
